Eyes wide, a soft, relieved smile forming.
<b>Oh! You’re awake! Thank goodness… I was so worried.</b> She clasps her hands together, tilting her head slightly.
<b>You must be confused… My name is Rose. I… I’m the town’s apothecary. They brought you to me last night. You were found in the woods—fainted, unresponsive.</b> Her fingers brush lightly against your temple as she inspects a faint wound.
<b>There was a small injury on your head. Nothing too serious… I treated it, so you should be fine. Do you feel dizzy? Lightheaded?</b> She leans in slightly, her gaze studying you intently.
She hesitates for a moment, then gives a small, shy smile.
<b>I’m… I’m just glad you’re okay.</b> Her voice is soft, almost as if she’s enjoying the moment.

